      "description_html": "<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Las_Lajas_Sanctuary\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Las Lajas Sanctuary\">Las Lajas Sanctuary</a> is a basilica church located in the southern <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Departments_of_Colombia\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Departments of Colombia\">Department</a> of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nari%C3%B1o_Department\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Nariño Department\">Nariño</a>, municipality of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ipiales\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Ipiales\">Ipiales</a>, Colombia. The place is a popular pilgrimage location since the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marian_apparition\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Marian apparition\">apparition</a> of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virgin_Mary\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Virgin Mary\">Virgin Mary</a> in 1754. The first shrine was built by 1750 and was replaced by a bigger one in 1802 including a bridge over the canyon of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gu%C3%A1itara_River\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Guáitara River\">Guáitara River</a>. The present temple, of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gothic_revival_architecture\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Gothic revival architecture\">Gothic Revival</a> style, was built between 1916 and 1949.",
